1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,297
Your skin sheds its outer
layer every few weeks,

2
00:00:03,297 --> 00:00:05,462
so why doesn't your tattoo shed with it?

3
00:00:05,767 --> 00:00:08,408
It's because the needle
puts the ink deeper,

4
00:00:08,408 --> 00:00:12,550
where immune cells called macrophages
swallow it but can't digest it,

5
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:14,170
so they just hold on to it.

6
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:19,371
So when scientists killed those cells in
tattooed mice, the tattoos didn't fade,

7
00:00:19,371 --> 00:00:23,110
because new cells swallowed the
spilled ink in the same spot.

8
00:00:23,417 --> 00:00:26,918
And that's why lasers take so
many sessions to remove a tattoo,

9
00:00:26,918 --> 00:00:31,420
since they have to shatter the ink small
enough for those cells to carry it away.
